## 5. Environment and infrastructure

### ENV-1 · CI has never been observed green · OPEN
The remote exists and `main`, `staging` and both tags are pushed, so the
blocking half of this is gone. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` is valid YAML with
2 jobs and 17 steps, but validity is not the same as passing and no run has
been watched.

- Needed: confirm the first run is green and fix whatever it finds.
- Until then every "all gates pass" claim rests on local runs only.

### ENV-2 · Vercel CLI not installed · YOURS
`npm i -g vercel` then `vercel login && vercel link`. README.md and
DEVELOPMENT.md both document `npm run env:pull`, which cannot work until then.

### ENV-3 · MCP servers unavailable · YOURS
- `vercel` and `supabase` need OAuth, which cannot run in a non-interactive
  session — authorise via claude.ai connector settings or `/mcp`.
- `github` fails with "Authorization header is badly formatted" — a
  connection fault in its configured token, not a missing capability.

### ENV-4 · Git identity may misattribute commits · YOURS
Commits are authored as `jacob.frusher@cil-uk.co.uk`; the account email here
is `jacob@frusher.co.uk`. Which one this repository should carry is your
call, so it was left as is. If GitHub does not list the work address on your
account, either add it there or run
`git config user.email jacob@frusher.co.uk` in this repository.

### ENV-5 · Branch protection not configured · YOURS
DEVELOPMENT.md §5.6 specifies protecting `main` and `staging`, with the CI
checks required. Also set GitHub's default branch to `main`. Until then the
branching model is a convention rather than a rule.

